  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refugee and Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) Profiling Towards Sustainable Peace and Durable Solutions in Darfur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support the implementation of the Juba Peace Agreement (JPA), its provisions on internally displaced persons (IDP) and refugees, and their right of return and integration in West, North and Central Darfur, Sudan. This will be achieved through profiling, perception, and intentions studies, and the collection of disaggregated data on the needs, vulnerabilities, and capabilities of IDPs and refugees compared with those of nomads and non-displaced communities. This is notably important to inform area-based programming that is conflict-sensitive and supports social cohesion in areas of return and integration.</narrative>
  </description>
